---
description: Routes work to the Agent Skills in .cursor/skills
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository keeps its hard-won knowledge in Agent Skills at `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`,
not in these rules. Open the matching one **before** starting the work rather than after something
breaks: each exists because that area has a trap not visible from the code around it.

Two unrelated things here are called skills. `.cursor/skills/` is for you, working on this
repository. `src/skills/` ships to Jarvis's own model at runtime. A request to "add a skill" is
ambiguous until you know which is meant.

- **`add-agent-tool`** — before adding, changing or removing a tool the model can call.
- **`debug-model-output`** — before touching the parser, the agent loop, the worker or the
  generation config, and whenever explaining a reply that came out wrong.
- **`write-model-skill`** — before adding or changing anything under `src/skills/`.
- **`ui-components`** — before writing or editing a React component.
- **`verify-in-browser`** — before claiming anything about installation, caching, offline behaviour
  or model quality.
- **`ship-a-change`** — before committing, opening a PR, cutting a release, or editing the build or
  the workflows.

Two things apply to every change:

- Finish with `pnpm check`. When it fails on formatting run `pnpm format`; never hand-fix it.
- Do not claim the model works unless it ran on a real GPU in Chrome or Edge. There is no CPU
  fallback, and `pnpm test` cannot reach the model at all.
